  "caption": "Quinn dived for a mark at footy, the shoulder popped out and then popped back in. Sorted? The next day it felt sore, wobbly and untrustworthy.\n\nA first dislocation can happen again, especially in younger athletes, and age at the first dislocation is one of the strongest predictors of repeats. \"It went back in\" doesn't mean it doesn't need checking.\n\nWhat can help: a proper medical review, early gentle movement in safe ranges, progressive rotator cuff and shoulder-blade strength, and testing strength and confidence before returning to sport.\n\nSeek urgent care if you notice numbness or weakness in the arm, or the shoulder won't go back in cleanly.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
